From 448570c72f65f611fccdc71507661572a5e17260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 16:36:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/52] kaiair: T0.3, runtime-tunable PktR knobs via
 KAIAIR_PKTR_* env

Make gamma, beta, the interference-EWMA memory c, and the regime-transition
sigma threshold tunable between gNB runs without recompiling, so beta/c can be
swept on hardware. Defaults match pktr_config (gamma=3, beta=0.99, c=15/16,
sigma_transient=6), so behavior is unchanged when nothing is set.

- pktr_runtime_config.h (new): process-wide pktr_settings loaded once from
  KAIAIR_PKTR_{METRICS,GAMMA_DB,BETA,EWMA_C,SIGMA_TRANSIENT_DB}, clamped to sane
  ranges (beta,c in [0,1); sigma>=0). detail::load_pktr_settings() exposed for tests.
- ue_cell + scheduler metrics handler: construct their pktr_link_state with the
  configured EWMA c instead of the hardcoded default.
- view: read gamma/beta/c/sigma-threshold from the runtime config (env flag now
  delegates here too); print an active "[config]" line so the operating values
  are visible in the feedback block.
- pktr_runtime_config_test (new, 5 cases): defaults, parsing, bad-value fallback,
  clamping, metrics-flag semantics.

Chose env vars over a gNB-YAML section for this round because c is a
scheduler-internal knob that a view-only YAML path can't reach without threading
config through the scheduler-config plumbing; the YAML `pktr:` section is the
planned productization (T0.3b) once good operating values are found.

Verified on the ARA gNB container: pktr_{link_state,ipc,runtime_config}_test pass;
scheduler_test 100% (no regression); gnb links clean.
